{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.SkeinCoulombEnhancement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.SkeinCoulombEnhancement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_coulomb_enhancement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_coulomb_enhancement","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L245-L249","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skein-coulomb-enhancement","label":"prop:skein-coulomb-enhancement","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_monotone_eta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_monotone_eta","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L162-L243","doc":"The enhancement factor grows with Z (more protons = stronger\nCoulomb field = larger enhancement). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sommerfeldParam_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sommerfeldParam_pos","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L145-L160","doc":"The Sommerfeld parameter is positive when q > 1, Z > 0, β_e > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_limit_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_limit_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L76-L143","doc":"The physical statement: lim_{η→0⁺} F_q(η) = 1.\nThis is the correct formulation of F(0) = 1 since the pointwise\nevaluation gives 0/0 = 0 in Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L66-L74","doc":"At η = 0 the formula gives 0/0, which Lean evaluates to 0 by\nconvention (division by zero returns 0 in ℝ).  The physically\nmeaningful statement is the limit lim_{η→0⁺} F(η) = 1, proved\nin `skeinCoulombFactor_limit_one` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L42-L64","doc":"The enhancement factor is ≥ 1 for η > 0 (β⁻ decay).\nThe Coulomb field of the daughter nucleus attracts the emitted\nelectron, increasing the wave function overlap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinCoulombFactor","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L36-L40","doc":"The Skein-Coulomb enhancement factor:\nF_q(Z, E) = 2πη / (1 - e^{-2πη}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sommerfeldParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sommerfeldParam","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/skein-coulomb-enhancement.lean#L29-L34","doc":"The q-deformed Sommerfeld parameter: η_q = α_q · Z / β_e\nwhere α_q = (q - q⁻¹) · λ_α is the fine structure constant\nfrom the crossing asymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}